{
 "title": "Elizabeth Holmes: The Theranos Verdict — Guilty on Investors, Not Guilty on Patients",
 "summary": "January 3, 2022: a federal jury in San Jose finds Theranos founder Elizabeth Holmes guilty of defrauding investors — and not guilty of defrauding patients. Built from the indictment, the verdict form, the government's sentencing memorandum, the judge's orders and the Ninth Circuit's opinion, this is what investors were told, what was really happening inside Theranos, how the jury split, why Judge Edward Davila imposed 135 months — and why that sentence was cut in 2026.",
